                  "layoutGrow": 1,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "1:748",
                      "name": "FAQ Item",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 0,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 121,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": [
                        "Do I need to know Kubernetes?",
                        "One-time cluster setup benefits from basic Helm familiarity. Day-to-day server management — console, files, backups, players — is entirely dashboard-driven; kubectl is optional."
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1:759",
                      "name": "FAQ Item",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 137,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 121,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": [
                        "Is Gameplane production-ready?",
                        "It's a pre-v1 release (v0.4.0). Core workflows are feature-complete and tested, but not yet recommended for unattended production — see the Roadmap."
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1:760",
                      "name": "FAQ Item",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 274,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 103,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": ["Is it free?", "Yes. Gameplane is open-source under AGPL-3.0-or-later, with no paid tiers."]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "1:761",
                  "name": "frame",
                  "type": "FRAME",
                  "x": 564,
                  "y": 0,
                  "width": 532,
                  "height": 496,
                  "layout": {
                    "mode": "VERTICAL",
                    "gap": 16,
                    "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                    "primary": "MIN",
                    "counter": "MIN",
                    "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                  },
                  "layoutGrow": 1,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "1:762",
                      "name": "FAQ Item",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 0,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 103,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": [
                        "What happens to my data if I uninstall?",
                        "Depends on your cluster's StorageClass reclaim policy — Gameplane doesn't force-delete PVCs itself. Back up critical data before uninstalling."
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1:763",
                      "name": "FAQ Item",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 119,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 121,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": [
                        "What database does it use?",
                        "SQLite by default and is the production-tested driver. The PostgreSQL driver works end to end but is experimental: it needs an API image built with the `postgres` build tag, and the API must stay a single replica."
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1:764",
                      "name": "FAQ Item",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 256,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 103,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": [
                        "Can I manage servers without the dashboard?",
                        "Yes. Advanced users can bypass the API entirely and manage everything with kubectl apply — the operator is authoritative, so both stay in sync."
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1:765",
                      "name": "FAQ Item Dashboard Cluster",
                      "type": "INSTANCE",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 375,
                      "width": 532,
                      "height": 121,
                      "component": "Accordion/Open",
                      "componentId": "1:749",
                      "layout": {
                        "mode": "VERTICAL",
                        "gap": 0,
                        "padding": [0, 0, 0, 0],
                        "primary": "MIN",
                        "counter": "MIN",
                        "sizing": ["HUG", "FIXED"]
                      },
                      "layoutAlignSelf": "STRETCH",
                      "texts": [
                        "Do I need a Kubernetes cluster to run the dashboard?",
                        "Not for the panel itself since v0.4.0. Docker Compose or a standalone Helm profile runs the API and dashboard without Kubernetes; games still run on registered clusters, each with its own operator and agents."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
